{
  "about": "A key unlocks only from what the visitor carries: not from the flagstones or the open crate, from the hand and from the open pouch, not through it shut; a key carried is meant over one lying further out; `open … with` holds its slot to the rule; and `put`'s container, not carried, is the crate on the floor.",
